WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.791
- It's always worth it to do your best,

00:00:02.791 --> 00:00:04.493
and to believe in something,

00:00:04.493 --> 00:00:07.170
and to work towards the
attainment of the goal.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.160
There's a saying that says,

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.916
"You could lead a horse to the water,"

00:00:09.916 --> 00:00:11.198
- [Interviewer] But you can't...

00:00:11.198 --> 00:00:12.676
- "But you can't make them drink."

00:00:12.676 --> 00:00:14.580
Plan, you plan.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.065
"But what about if this comes up?"

00:00:16.065 --> 00:00:17.730
You don't get caught off guard.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.295
Proper preparation
prevents poor performance.

00:00:20.295 --> 00:00:21.533
You know, if you work hard,

00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:23.866
and your work is recognized,

00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:27.653
you know, the sky's the limit.

00:00:27.653 --> 00:00:29.903
- He's an American
professional body builder,

00:00:29.903 --> 00:00:32.570
personal trainer, artist and actor.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:36.182
His most recent victory was
the 2016 Arnold Classic.

00:00:36.182 --> 00:00:39.455
He also came second
place in the 2012, 2013,

00:00:39.455 --> 00:00:41.840
and 2014 Mr. Olympia.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:42.798
He's Kai Greene,

00:00:42.798 --> 00:00:45.644
and here's my take on his
top ten rules for success.

00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:47.197
Rule #2 is my personal favorite,

00:00:47.197 --> 00:00:48.772
and make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:48.772 --> 00:00:50.224
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:50.224 --> 00:00:51.371
Also, once Kai is talking,

00:00:51.371 --> 00:00:53.441
if he says something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:53.441 --> 00:00:55.016
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:55.016 --> 00:00:55.927
and put quotes around it

00:00:55.927 --> 00:00:58.133
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:58.966
Enjoy.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.983
(uplifting music)

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.721
- 2015 Mr. Olympia is

00:01:15.729 --> 00:01:17.562
fastly approaching and

00:01:20.779 --> 00:01:22.112
I am regrettably

00:01:26.474 --> 00:01:28.807
of the realization that I am

00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:32.549
not going to be allowed to compete.

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:35.069
Let me just say that I have,

00:01:35.069 --> 00:01:38.658
I have invested more
than 20 years of my life

00:01:38.658 --> 00:01:41.269
in the belief in the idea

00:01:41.269 --> 00:01:43.383
of being able to come to the Olympia,

00:01:43.383 --> 00:01:45.633
and to do an absolute best,

00:01:47.017 --> 00:01:49.425
despite whatever the opposition,

00:01:49.425 --> 00:01:51.483
whatever's said,

00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:53.566
whatever the beliefs are,

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:56.310
onstage, offstage,

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.977
whatever the oppositionary
forces have been,

00:02:00.877 --> 00:02:04.253
my resolve has been to
respond as a champion,

00:02:04.253 --> 00:02:05.503
and just aim to

00:02:07.077 --> 00:02:11.244
represent the better thought
of what that means to me.

00:02:14.086 --> 00:02:16.003
You don't get this far,

00:02:17.045 --> 00:02:20.049
you don't get to this point,

00:02:20.049 --> 00:02:21.216
and just stop.

00:02:27.429 --> 00:02:31.596
(sniffs) It doesn't happen like that.

00:02:37.049 --> 00:02:37.882
I am...

00:02:38.859 --> 00:02:41.887
I'm not a victim, I'm not a...

00:02:41.887 --> 00:02:44.054
They ain't going to break me,

00:02:45.497 --> 00:02:47.579
and I don't want to speak
negatively at anybody.

00:02:47.579 --> 00:02:49.570
I don't want to speak negatively
about anything, you know.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.699
Let me just say that
there's more going on than,

00:02:52.699 --> 00:02:54.449
than I'm able to say.

00:03:01.833 --> 00:03:03.750
(sobs)

00:03:14.502 --> 00:03:15.669
It's not fair.

00:03:16.639 --> 00:03:18.056
I can't say that.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.249
What they're doing,

00:03:22.174 --> 00:03:24.203
what's being done,

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.536
why it's actually happening,

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.673
it is what it is.

00:03:31.673 --> 00:03:34.498
You know, we talk about
overcoming objections,

00:03:34.498 --> 00:03:35.865
and a lot of times we don't know exactly

00:03:35.865 --> 00:03:38.948
what those objections will be,

00:03:38.948 --> 00:03:40.297
and sometimes they can come up,

00:03:40.297 --> 00:03:42.998
and they can be so overwhelming that,

00:03:42.998 --> 00:03:46.811
wow, we didn't anticipate
that, we didn't know,

00:03:46.811 --> 00:03:47.978
but we just...

00:03:48.916 --> 00:03:50.468
We got to still aim to do,

00:03:50.468 --> 00:03:52.077
and still believe and recognize

00:03:52.077 --> 00:03:54.827
that there are things that are...

00:03:58.816 --> 00:04:01.257
It's always worth it to do your best,

00:04:01.257 --> 00:04:03.024
and to believe in something,

00:04:03.024 --> 00:04:05.994
and to work towards the
attainment of the goal,

00:04:05.994 --> 00:04:06.994
and if it is

00:04:13.297 --> 00:04:16.297
that you have to expand your vision,

00:04:17.447 --> 00:04:19.078
then you climb higher and you do that,

00:04:19.078 --> 00:04:21.328
and you don't be afraid to.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:28.223
2015 Olympia weekend is going to come

00:04:40.094 --> 00:04:42.177
(sniffs)

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.513
I am a champion,

00:04:46.946 --> 00:04:47.863
as are you,

00:04:49.837 --> 00:04:50.754
not because

00:04:52.606 --> 00:04:54.856
of the trophies and titles,

00:04:55.935 --> 00:04:59.727
but because of the
obstacles that you overcome,

00:04:59.727 --> 00:05:02.144
and the effort that you exert

00:05:04.193 --> 00:05:06.184
to find what it is to be your best,

00:05:06.184 --> 00:05:08.524
and to aim to do it

00:05:08.524 --> 00:05:09.897
because you decide to,

00:05:09.897 --> 00:05:14.701
and recognize that it
is your right (sniffs),

00:05:14.701 --> 00:05:17.233
and your responsibility to do so.

00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:19.764
There's a lot of work
that we're responsible for

00:05:19.764 --> 00:05:21.369
that other people can't do,

00:05:21.369 --> 00:05:22.202
you know.

00:05:22.202 --> 00:05:24.057
There's a saying that says,

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:26.318
"You can lead a horse to the water,"

00:05:26.318 --> 00:05:27.151
- [Interviewer] But you can't...

00:05:27.151 --> 00:05:28.737
- "But you can't make them drink."

00:05:28.737 --> 00:05:31.843
In the presence of common
sense and rational thinking,

00:05:31.843 --> 00:05:33.946
when even in the throes of your despair,

00:05:33.946 --> 00:05:35.284
it is your responsibility,

00:05:35.284 --> 00:05:38.446
if you are willing to still commit

00:05:38.446 --> 00:05:40.446
to saving your own life,

00:05:41.542 --> 00:05:42.699
to hear that,

00:05:42.699 --> 00:05:45.320
and just walk towards
that voice, you know.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.403
So, you know,

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:52.667
I want to recognize personal
responsibility, you know,

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.917
and in what we try to do here today,

00:05:54.917 --> 00:05:56.503
one of things that make, you know,

00:05:56.503 --> 00:05:59.420
body building a significant vehicle

00:06:00.374 --> 00:06:03.433
for therapy, and maybe even a tool,

00:06:03.433 --> 00:06:05.808
you know, towards personal development

00:06:05.808 --> 00:06:06.899
is just that.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.890
You know, in order to be
able to do this effectively,

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.894
you have to recognize your
personal responsibility.

00:06:11.894 --> 00:06:13.477
So, with that said,

00:06:14.515 --> 00:06:15.697
you know,

00:06:15.697 --> 00:06:19.556
I am going to submit to
you that the word believe,

00:06:19.556 --> 00:06:21.063
believe is work.

00:06:21.063 --> 00:06:24.063
You can substitute work for believe,

00:06:25.564 --> 00:06:26.497
you know, because when I'm working,

00:06:26.497 --> 00:06:28.207
what are you working for?

00:06:28.207 --> 00:06:29.782
If you're working without a belief

00:06:29.782 --> 00:06:31.391
in the idea that you going to get paid,

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:34.024
then what is your work for?

00:06:34.024 --> 00:06:35.936
What is the purpose?

00:06:35.936 --> 00:06:38.353
So, I believe that, you know,

00:06:39.728 --> 00:06:41.090
to talk about believing is to talk

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.002
about being willing to do the work.

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:45.502
First, let me say that I think

00:06:46.614 --> 00:06:48.697
the goals pretty much set

00:06:51.808 --> 00:06:54.170
the tone for everything else.

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:55.003
So,

00:06:57.073 --> 00:06:57.906
you know,

00:07:01.146 --> 00:07:04.469
I guess when you think about goal setting,

00:07:04.469 --> 00:07:08.219
and when you really
allow your goals to start

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.468
becoming the lead

00:07:12.468 --> 00:07:14.167
to manage your steps,

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:17.167
then your life path starts to become

00:07:19.522 --> 00:07:21.054
guided,

00:07:21.054 --> 00:07:22.971
and not just haphazard,

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:26.787
and by chance.

00:07:30.277 --> 00:07:34.027
You're goals become the
predetermined address

00:07:36.758 --> 00:07:39.425
that will serve as a destination

00:07:41.521 --> 00:07:43.490
and end result,

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:44.323
and now,

00:07:45.312 --> 00:07:47.281
with at least that,

00:07:47.281 --> 00:07:51.448
you're able to make decisions
and map out a course,

00:07:53.165 --> 00:07:55.730
step by step if you will,

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:57.980
that will help get you there.

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:00.399
The really cool thing about

00:08:00.399 --> 00:08:01.490
goal setting is that

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:05.619
even if you do not have
all the information

00:08:05.619 --> 00:08:07.858
beyond the address,

00:08:07.858 --> 00:08:11.358
like what streets, when and where to turn,

00:08:13.281 --> 00:08:15.159
with having the address,

00:08:15.159 --> 00:08:18.326
you can always type in GPS coordinate,

00:08:20.087 --> 00:08:22.837
and pretty much take advantage of

00:08:24.351 --> 00:08:26.883
other sensibilities
that can help point you

00:08:26.883 --> 00:08:29.324
in the right direction.

00:08:29.324 --> 00:08:32.024
A lot of times, you
don't really need to have

00:08:32.024 --> 00:08:34.792
all of the guess work predetermined

00:08:34.792 --> 00:08:36.682
and already figured out,

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:39.157
once you have the address,

00:08:39.157 --> 00:08:41.521
you're that much closer

00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:45.064
to being able to get
where you're trying to go.

00:08:45.064 --> 00:08:46.898
As an athlete on stage,

00:08:46.898 --> 00:08:49.914
that's kind of what I'm using to

00:08:49.914 --> 00:08:50.831
help get me

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.323
where I feel I need to be

00:08:54.323 --> 00:08:57.406
to perform at the maximum efficiency.

00:09:01.849 --> 00:09:05.551
So, yeah, goal setting is
very, very, very important,

00:09:05.551 --> 00:09:09.718
and it's been very, very
critical in helping me get

00:09:11.075 --> 00:09:14.349
from the beginning of my career

00:09:14.349 --> 00:09:16.250
to where I am presently.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:18.320
Still don't feel like you've quite arrived

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.512
at the right answer, right?

00:09:20.512 --> 00:09:21.345
You know, is this...

00:09:21.345 --> 00:09:23.109
"Okay, should I do three
of these, or is it six?

00:09:23.109 --> 00:09:26.158
"Or is it 45 minutes, or is it an hour?

00:09:26.158 --> 00:09:27.600
"So I just go ahead and finish, you know,

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.252
"get the two-hour session in.

00:09:29.252 --> 00:09:30.208
"Hey, I feel this way.

00:09:30.208 --> 00:09:31.041
"Do I need to stop?

00:09:31.041 --> 00:09:32.267
"No, you know what, I
know I feel this way,

00:09:32.267 --> 00:09:33.369
"but I need to continue.

00:09:33.369 --> 00:09:34.753
"Is it healthier for me to stop?

00:09:34.753 --> 00:09:36.317
"Oh no, no, I'm good, I'm good, I got it.

00:09:36.317 --> 00:09:37.510
"Let me continue, let me push it.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:38.590
"I know I said I was only going to have

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:39.827
"this many grams of carbs today,

00:09:39.827 --> 00:09:41.042
"but is that light-headedness,

00:09:41.042 --> 00:09:43.945
"or is it that I just
really want more carbs?"

00:09:43.945 --> 00:09:46.191
It's troubleshooting all day.

00:09:46.191 --> 00:09:47.656
"Should I take an extra
two grams of protein?

00:09:47.656 --> 00:09:48.578
"Will it really matter?

00:09:48.578 --> 00:09:49.411
"How much sodium?

00:09:49.411 --> 00:09:51.083
"Dammit, you know, you
can't eat out anymore.

00:09:51.083 --> 00:09:52.635
"I have two meals with
me and then, you know,

00:09:52.635 --> 00:09:54.638
"the rest, you know, I can eat out

00:09:54.638 --> 00:09:55.763
for these next two meals."

00:09:55.763 --> 00:09:57.844
No, you cook every meal.

00:09:57.844 --> 00:09:59.779
You prepare for all day.

00:09:59.779 --> 00:10:03.064
Your steps do not happen
randomly by chance.

00:10:03.064 --> 00:10:04.966
Plan, you plan.

00:10:04.966 --> 00:10:06.327
"But what about if this comes up?"

00:10:06.327 --> 00:10:08.082
You don't get caught off guard.

00:10:08.082 --> 00:10:10.985
Proper preparation
prevents poor performance.

00:10:10.985 --> 00:10:15.166
It's your responsibility
to plan, to prepare.

00:10:15.166 --> 00:10:16.708
This is your dream.

00:10:16.708 --> 00:10:19.622
The achieving great
things though comes from,

00:10:19.622 --> 00:10:20.455
you know,

00:10:21.447 --> 00:10:24.771
the ability to manage yourself
very, very, very well,

00:10:24.771 --> 00:10:27.786
you know, or at least well enough

00:10:27.786 --> 00:10:29.170
where you almost become compulsive

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:32.003
about getting certain things done,

00:10:32.882 --> 00:10:33.715
you know.

00:10:34.727 --> 00:10:36.550
You have to set a standard for yourself

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:38.856
that is very, very, very high,

00:10:38.856 --> 00:10:39.689
you know,

00:10:40.803 --> 00:10:43.210
and you have to manage yourself

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:46.192
to keep your thoughts
where they need to be

00:10:46.192 --> 00:10:48.183
in order to allow you

00:10:48.183 --> 00:10:51.378
to be successful at what
you're trying to do.

00:10:51.378 --> 00:10:54.371
One way you can say "Absolutely, I can,"

00:10:54.371 --> 00:10:58.094
is not with your mouth,
but with your actions,

00:10:58.094 --> 00:10:59.737
and actions are the product of thought,

00:10:59.737 --> 00:11:03.011
so if you're continuing to think

00:11:03.011 --> 00:11:04.800
like I was saying when we were training,

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.633
"Am I doing this as good as I can?

00:11:08.535 --> 00:11:10.482
"Can I command more from myself?

00:11:10.482 --> 00:11:12.867
"Am I connecting with this muscle

00:11:12.867 --> 00:11:16.029
"as intensely as I can connect?

00:11:16.029 --> 00:11:17.851
"Am I training hard enough?"

00:11:17.851 --> 00:11:20.012
You know, "Can I train harder?"

00:11:20.012 --> 00:11:22.992
Obstacles really don't matter.

00:11:22.992 --> 00:11:24.909
They really just don't,

00:11:26.986 --> 00:11:29.708
no more than where you come from,

00:11:29.708 --> 00:11:33.669
what you had, what you
have, what you didn't have.

00:11:33.669 --> 00:11:36.932
All that stuff becomes so what?

00:11:36.932 --> 00:11:38.182
People that are

00:11:39.656 --> 00:11:40.823
concerned with

00:11:43.131 --> 00:11:43.964
results,

00:11:44.987 --> 00:11:47.627
and the person that's working

00:11:47.627 --> 00:11:51.991
with their mind fixed on
the end result being success

00:11:51.991 --> 00:11:53.158
are a lot less

00:11:56.075 --> 00:11:58.235
concerned about the problems,

00:11:58.235 --> 00:12:02.263
and they're more willing
to explore solutions,

00:12:02.263 --> 00:12:04.596
and if need be, create them.

00:12:05.942 --> 00:12:09.859
That is, probably, the
best use of your energy.

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:17.057
Arnold Schwarzenegger was
said to once give a seminar

00:12:17.057 --> 00:12:17.890
somewhere.

00:12:19.364 --> 00:12:22.697
I think they reference it in either the,

00:12:23.605 --> 00:12:25.900
the book The Education of a Bodybuilder,

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:30.067
or Arnold Schwarzenegger's
Encyclopedia of Bodybuilding.

00:12:32.695 --> 00:12:36.983
One time giving a
seminar, it was said that,

00:12:36.983 --> 00:12:38.233
he talked about

00:12:40.133 --> 00:12:41.883
focusing on his goal,

00:12:43.238 --> 00:12:45.600
and how the only time you can begin

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:49.350
to really assess the
enormity of an obstacle,

00:12:52.745 --> 00:12:56.828
was to have to first take
your eye off your goal.

00:13:00.327 --> 00:13:02.725
That's the end of my Arnold
Schwarzenegger quote,

00:13:02.725 --> 00:13:06.475
but I guess in recalling
that at this moment,

00:13:08.507 --> 00:13:11.207
what I realize is, you know,

00:13:11.207 --> 00:13:12.290
if I'm an NFL

00:13:15.407 --> 00:13:17.281
outside linebacker looking to try

00:13:17.281 --> 00:13:19.013
to put a sack on the quarterback

00:13:19.013 --> 00:13:20.763
of the opposing team,

00:13:23.423 --> 00:13:25.673
if I am looking at the size

00:13:28.071 --> 00:13:30.940
of the lineman in front of me

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:34.563
looking to stop me, the
defenders looking to stop me

00:13:34.563 --> 00:13:36.869
from getting to the quarterback,

00:13:36.869 --> 00:13:38.625
if I start taking into account,

00:13:38.625 --> 00:13:40.200
"Wow, how big is his hands," and

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.024
"How much does this guy weigh," and

00:13:43.024 --> 00:13:46.035
"Man, look at the size of his neck,"

00:13:46.035 --> 00:13:47.454
chances are,

00:13:47.454 --> 00:13:50.017
in order to make all of those assessments,

00:13:50.017 --> 00:13:53.482
I can't be looking at the
quarterback behind him anymore,

00:13:53.482 --> 00:13:56.565
and if my responsibility in this play

00:13:57.679 --> 00:13:59.778
was to put pressure on the quarterback,

00:13:59.778 --> 00:14:01.893
and even better,

00:14:01.893 --> 00:14:03.558
put my hands on the quarterback,

00:14:03.558 --> 00:14:06.806
cause a fumble to stop the play,

00:14:06.806 --> 00:14:09.539
then I'm going to be rendered ineffective,

00:14:09.539 --> 00:14:12.217
not by anything the lineman has done,

00:14:12.217 --> 00:14:14.962
but because I have now
taken my eye off of the goal

00:14:14.962 --> 00:14:16.462
in order to assess

00:14:17.392 --> 00:14:21.559
the size and weight of the
obstacle in front of me.

00:14:23.141 --> 00:14:25.031
Successful people,

00:14:25.031 --> 00:14:28.586
I imagine, have to worry less about

00:14:28.586 --> 00:14:31.253
what the size of the obstacles are,

00:14:31.253 --> 00:14:33.379
the finances or the lack thereof,

00:14:33.379 --> 00:14:36.712
and all the other things that we can say

00:14:37.902 --> 00:14:41.902
represent the size and
weight of the opposition.

00:14:44.573 --> 00:14:46.869
What the successful person
is going to aim to do,

00:14:46.869 --> 00:14:51.036
and what all of us that
would like to be successful

00:14:52.021 --> 00:14:55.149
would, probably, want to adopt

00:14:55.149 --> 00:14:58.149
as a part of our philosophy would be

00:15:00.493 --> 00:15:02.630
to worry less about the obstacles,

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.547
and fix our thoughts on

00:15:06.311 --> 00:15:07.660
the goal.

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:09.696
It's one thing to philosophize

00:15:09.696 --> 00:15:12.936
about training strategies and to,

00:15:12.936 --> 00:15:13.769
you know,

00:15:15.782 --> 00:15:19.032
compare this philosophy versus another,

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:21.363
you know,

00:15:22.881 --> 00:15:26.257
argue about, you know, how many grams

00:15:26.257 --> 00:15:28.507
versus how many grams is...

00:15:29.609 --> 00:15:30.802
But then there's something to be said

00:15:30.802 --> 00:15:33.266
about doing the damn thing.

00:15:33.266 --> 00:15:34.099
You know,

00:15:34.099 --> 00:15:35.016
just do it.

00:15:37.541 --> 00:15:40.050
You know, stop talking,

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:41.558
stop trying to sound smart.

00:15:41.558 --> 00:15:44.167
You meet these people
that want to engage you

00:15:44.167 --> 00:15:45.709
in these conversations,

00:15:45.709 --> 00:15:47.754
and one-up the professional body builder.

00:15:47.754 --> 00:15:49.970
"Ah, I know more about nutrition,"

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:52.137
well then, dude, I mean...

00:15:53.447 --> 00:15:54.286
I'm not...

00:15:54.286 --> 00:15:55.119
Straight.

00:15:56.173 --> 00:15:57.992
I'm not where I'm at because

00:15:57.992 --> 00:16:00.872
I know more about nutrition

00:16:00.872 --> 00:16:03.663
than everybody else on the planet.

00:16:03.663 --> 00:16:06.413
You know, in fact, I daresay that

00:16:07.298 --> 00:16:10.751
the top body building
athletes that are onstage

00:16:10.751 --> 00:16:12.843
are not the man onstage...

00:16:12.843 --> 00:16:14.294
You make a right here.

00:16:14.294 --> 00:16:18.461
Because they know more about
training science and nutrition

00:16:23.116 --> 00:16:25.405
than the average person
sitting in the audience.

00:16:25.405 --> 00:16:27.005
A lot of time, the
difference between the person

00:16:27.005 --> 00:16:30.064
in the audience and the person
that's onstage doing it,

00:16:30.064 --> 00:16:33.136
is the use of the knowledge.

00:16:33.136 --> 00:16:35.813
Success is not based on genetics.

00:16:35.813 --> 00:16:39.888
It's not based on how nice this car is.

00:16:39.888 --> 00:16:43.308
It's not based on how pretty my face is,

00:16:43.308 --> 00:16:46.447
how small my nose may need to look,

00:16:46.447 --> 00:16:47.280
or, you know,

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.981
whether or not I'm the right complexion.

00:16:49.981 --> 00:16:52.400
I have an eight inch scar
down the side of my face,

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.515
but I have a camera in front of me

00:16:54.515 --> 00:16:56.182
more often than not,

00:16:57.294 --> 00:16:59.127
which just means that, you know,

00:16:59.127 --> 00:17:00.275
if you work hard,

00:17:00.275 --> 00:17:02.608
and your work is recognized,

00:17:04.303 --> 00:17:06.429
you know, the sky's the limit.

00:17:06.429 --> 00:17:07.262
For all those people out there

00:17:07.262 --> 00:17:08.927
that think they're ugly and everything,

00:17:08.927 --> 00:17:13.297
Ima hold it down for you, but
more importantly, you know,

00:17:13.297 --> 00:17:15.007
you can still be a success.

00:17:15.007 --> 00:17:15.840
For all those people that think,

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:16.766
"Well, I'm too short,"

00:17:16.766 --> 00:17:19.349
well, I'm holding down for you.

00:17:20.242 --> 00:17:22.346
More importantly, you
can still be a success.

00:17:22.346 --> 00:17:25.449
Find the things that you're excited about,

00:17:25.449 --> 00:17:26.712
and that you can give your all,

00:17:26.712 --> 00:17:31.167
and you can work really
hard towards attaining.

00:17:31.167 --> 00:17:33.113
String those days of efficiency,

00:17:33.113 --> 00:17:34.846
efficient action together,

00:17:34.846 --> 00:17:36.950
and success can happen even for you.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.042
This is my life,

00:17:39.042 --> 00:17:41.585
but this is also me living it.

00:17:41.585 --> 00:17:42.585
You tune in,

00:17:43.891 --> 00:17:45.344
and what you should walk away from,

00:17:45.344 --> 00:17:48.479
what I would want you
most to walk away with,

00:17:48.479 --> 00:17:50.146
is the idea of, "Yo,

00:17:51.078 --> 00:17:53.159
"but what can I do?

00:17:53.159 --> 00:17:54.387
"What am I doing with my life?

00:17:54.387 --> 00:17:56.672
"Am I living it or am I just,

00:17:56.672 --> 00:17:58.347
"you know, going to some hum-drum job

00:17:58.347 --> 00:18:01.081
"that I don't really want to be at

00:18:01.081 --> 00:18:03.331
"doing some minuscule task,

00:18:04.422 --> 00:18:07.078
"getting paid to be a mindless drone,"

00:18:07.078 --> 00:18:07.911
you know,

00:18:07.911 --> 00:18:09.473
"Or am I out there living life

00:18:09.473 --> 00:18:11.128
"on my terms

00:18:11.128 --> 00:18:12.489
"they way I want to live it,

00:18:12.489 --> 00:18:14.413
"doing the things that I want to do?"

00:18:14.413 --> 00:18:15.313
Make no mistake about it.

00:18:15.313 --> 00:18:17.135
As hard as this is,

00:18:17.135 --> 00:18:19.025
as hard as this is,

00:18:19.025 --> 00:18:21.534
this is what I want to do.

00:18:21.534 --> 00:18:24.367
This is what I want to do, you know,

00:18:25.438 --> 00:18:28.241
and some people can make fun of it.

00:18:28.241 --> 00:18:29.208
They can crack jokes.

00:18:29.208 --> 00:18:30.895
They can sit back and analyze,

00:18:30.895 --> 00:18:32.729
and, you know,

00:18:32.729 --> 00:18:33.562
criticize,

00:18:34.438 --> 00:18:37.161
and make all the fun they want,

00:18:37.161 --> 00:18:39.130
but I'm living my life.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:40.997
I'm doing it.

00:18:40.997 --> 00:18:41.898
What are you?

00:18:41.898 --> 00:18:43.815
The mind is everything.

00:18:45.453 --> 00:18:47.379
If you don't believe you can do something,

00:18:47.379 --> 00:18:48.629
then you can't.

00:18:49.864 --> 00:18:53.115
If you believe that your father was a bum,

00:18:53.115 --> 00:18:54.993
and he left you,

00:18:54.993 --> 00:18:57.874
or your mother wasn't any good,

00:18:57.874 --> 00:19:01.665
if you believe that your
upbringing was substandard,

00:19:01.665 --> 00:19:03.994
and therefore, you have to walk around

00:19:03.994 --> 00:19:07.110
as a refugee from that crazy situation

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:08.415
for the rest of your life,

00:19:08.415 --> 00:19:09.665
forever bearing

00:19:13.051 --> 00:19:15.379
the burden of that experience,

00:19:15.379 --> 00:19:17.712
then that will be your life.

00:19:19.511 --> 00:19:22.928
It's like you have to save your own life.

00:19:26.293 --> 00:19:29.971
Nobody's going to be
able to save it for you,

00:19:29.971 --> 00:19:33.234
so we have to do what we have to do,

00:19:33.234 --> 00:19:34.984
no matter what it is.

